    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="1176" n="1162" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/9–1444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-03T20:00:00-04:00">October 3, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2656. The cable below is WRB 101. Please refer to your No. 2875 of September 14
                    (WRB 189).<anchor n="17" xml:id="d700-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>As you were advised in Department’s No. 2118 of July 28<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d700-f2"/> and 2332 of August 24,<anchor n="19" xml:id="d700-f3"/>
                    this Government has guaranteed that it will arrange for the maintenance in
                    Portugal and the removal to the United States or to other areas outside Portugal
                    of all refugees who are admitted to Portugal in accordance with the terms of
                    those cables. It is the firm intention of this Government to comply fully with
                    the terms of this guarantee, should the necessity arise. Until the number of
                    such refugees and other similar facts are known, it is neither possible nor
                    desirable to determine exactly where they will be taken. You may assume that all
                    available havens, including Fedhala, will be used to fulfill this Government’s
                    guarantee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
